  'Fragrant aged wine aromas of raisin bread, fruit cake, river rock', 'Walnut skin. Palate has more delicate notes of wheat malt, nutty oloroso', 'Subtle note of caramel & chocolate in the finish', 'Experimental Batch 021: Vatted High Malt. Column Still Mash Bill: Yellow Corn, Pale Malted Wheat, Caramel Malted Wheat, Oak Smoked Malted Wheat. Age: 4 years, 1 month. Proof: 100 (50% ALC/VOL). Cooperage: Charred Oak, 53 gallon. Finishing Cooperage: “Centenary" Oloroso Sherry Puncheon, 500 liter. Finishing Time: 3 mos. Batch Size: 1 barrel. Style: Straight Bourbon Whiskey Finished in an Oloroso Sherry Cask. Producer tasting note: "Fragrant aged wine aromas of raisin bread, fruit cake, river rock and walnut skin. Palate has more delicate notes of wheat malt and nutty oloroso, with a subtle note of caramel & chocolate in the finish." (nose/palate/finish above are an editorial split of that line).', now(), now());

