  'Maple, molasses, cocoa', 'Chocolate malt, a light smoky finish', 'Lingering a light smoky finish', 'Experimental Batch 003: Native Barrel (November, 2017). Mash Bill: Corn, Malted Rye, Caramel Malted Barley, Cherrywood Smoked Malted Barley. Age: 2+ years. Proof: 102 (51% ALC/VOL). Cooperage: Toasted & Charred Oak, 25 gallon. Finishing Cooperage: Smoked Doppelbock Beer Barrels, 53 gallon. Finishing Time: 1 month. Batch Size: 8 barrels. Style: Straight Bourbon Whiskey finished in Smoked Beer Barrels. Release Date: November, 2017. Smoke on Smoke. This collaborative batch takes Smoked High Malt (Batch 002), and finishes it in smoked doppelbock beer barrels from our friends at Odd Story Brewing Co. The malt used in the doppelbock was even smoked with corn cobs and oak staves from our distillery! Producer tasting note: "Maple, molasses, cocoa, chocolate malt and a light smoky finish" (nose/palate/finish above are an editorial split of that line). Tasting note is from the producer''s release announcement; the product page carries none.', now(), now());

